{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>In the most holy place you shall eat it.</b> The holy of holies (קדש הקדשים) is not the place of eating the offerings, for the place of the Ark is inside the curtain (פרוכת), as it is written (Exodus 26:33): ״והבדילה הפרכת לכם בין הקדש ובין קדש הקדשים״, and there is no eating or drinking in the holy of holies, for none enters there but the high priest on the Day of Atonement. But the meaning of the verse is: you shall eat it in strict sanctity, not conducting yourself with it according to the practice of lesser holy things (קדשים קלים), but it shall be among you most holy (קדש קדשים). Or we may say that קדש הקדשים is mentioned with reference to the Tent of Meeting (אהל מועד), and it is called קדש קדשים in contrast to the court of the Tabernacle."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:47.046333365Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}